{#- The page search (docs/features/navigation MENU-03, NAV-03, R3). Two instances, each with its own controllers on its root:
    - surface `bar`: the top bar's search field (templates/navigation/_topbar.html.twig, NAV-03) - the first instance in
      the DOM (tests read the first one). On phones a tap on it opens the search view (html[data-search-open], a
      GEST-01 layer: Back closes it): the field widens, × and - at 320-359 px - the scan button appear, the results
      panel (.site-search-panel) lies under the bar down to the bottom bar. On desktop the panel drops down under the
      field, no history entry (decision 22) - in the 768-1023 px bar the 🔍 (or Ctrl/Cmd+K) opens the field in the bar
      first; Ctrl/Cmd+K focuses it everywhere (NAV-04). The barcode scan sits in the field for members (from 360 px in
      the closed bar); everybody else gets the locked one only in the opened search (decision 21, never a teaser in the
      closed bar);
    - surface `menu` (key="menu"): the Menu panel's field (templates/navigation/_menu_layer.html.twig); its results show
      inside the panel - same layer, same history entry. No × (the panel has one; Esc clears the field first), the scan
      button only for members (rows a viewer cannot use are hidden, never locked - D13).
    Both are chrome: every button carries data-nav (P0-03).
    global-search: opening/closing (bar), Esc and the panel's searching state (menu); nav-search: "Pages & settings" -
    the registry's list (nav-search.json, fetched on the first focus) filtered and ranked in the browser
    (assets/navigation/nav_search.js) into the data-live-ignore container above the server results, which the Live
    re-renders never touch. An empty query renders no results and costs no statement.
    A member's scanner renders no camera of its own (the chrome's weight, README §4.12 - both instances are on every
    page): its wrapper stays empty until the first start, when barcode_scanner_controller.js copies the page's one
    camera markup in (`camera`: templates/navigation/_search_camera.html.twig, rendered by the top bar with the top bar's
    data-nav on its HUD; the Menu's copy gets menu/search/... - `hudNav`). The wrapper is data-live-ignore, so a Live
    re-render keeps that markup and the running camera, and it has an id, so a re-render that adds the results list in
    front of it never takes the list for it (idiomorph pairs elements by id first; without one the list was morphed out
    of the running camera's wrapper). position: relative comes from .global-search-barcode-scan (app.scss). -#}
{%- set menu = this.menu -%}
{%- set member = logged_user.profile is not null and logged_user.profile.activeMembership -%}
{%- set nav_surface = menu ? 'menu' : 'topbar' -%}
{#- SRCH-01: the top bar offers a guest the pages of any signed-in player as "Sign in to see …" (the same text for every
    guest - guest HTML stays shared) -#}
<div {{ attributes.defaults({
    class: menu ? 'global-search-menu' : 'global-search-bar site-search',
    'data-controller': 'global-search nav-search',
    'data-global-search-mode-value': this.surface,
    'data-nav-search-url-value': nav_search_url(),
    'data-nav-search-surface-value': this.surface,
    'data-nav-search-limit-value': this.limit,
    'data-nav-search-title-value': 'nav.search.pages_settings'|trans,
    'data-nav-search-more-value': 'nav.search.more'|trans,
}|merge(not menu and logged_user.profile is null ? {'data-nav-search-sign-in-value': 'nav.search.sign_in_to_see'|trans} : {})) }}>
    <div data-controller="barcode-scanner" data-barcode-scanner-no-camera-value="{{ 'barcode_scanner.no_camera'|trans }}"{% if member %} data-barcode-scanner-camera-value="search-camera"{% if menu %} data-barcode-scanner-hud-nav-value="menu/search"{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not menu %} class="site-search-box"{% endif %}>
        {% if menu %}
        <div class="input-group global-search-field">
            <input type="search" data-model="debounce(150)|query" class="form-control" autocomplete="off" aria-label="{{ 'menu.search'|trans }}" data-barcode-scanner-target="input" data-global-search-target="searchInput" data-nav-search-target="input" placeholder="{{ 'forms.global_search_placeholder'|trans }}">
            {% if member %}
                <button
                    class="btn btn-secondary border-0 px-3 fs-6"
                    data-action="click->barcode-scanner#toggle"
                    data-barcode-scanner-target="toggleButton"
                    aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.barcode_scanner'|trans }}"
                    data-nav="menu/search/scan"
                >
                    <i class="bi-upc-scan" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% else %}
        {#- The top bar's field: magnifier · the input (16 px, the one-word placeholder; on desktop
            global_search_controller.js puts the long one in whenever it fits the field - measured, again after a resize
            and after every Live re-render) · scan; × closes the opened search (phones and the 768-1023 px bar). -#}
        <div class="site-search-row">
            <div class="site-search-field">
                <svg class="site-search-glass" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#nav-i-search"/></svg>
                <input type="search" data-model="debounce(150)|query" class="site-search-input" autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="search"
                       aria-label="{{ 'nav.bar.search_label'|trans }}" placeholder="{{ 'nav.bar.search_placeholder'|trans }}"
                       data-placeholder-short="{{ 'nav.bar.search_placeholder'|trans }}" data-placeholder-long="{{ 'nav.bar.search_placeholder_long'|trans }}"
                       data-barcode-scanner-target="input" data-global-search-target="searchInput" data-nav-search-target="input">
                {% if member %}
                    <button type="button" class="site-search-scan"
                            data-action="click->global-search#openView click->barcode-scanner#toggle"
                            data-barcode-scanner-target="toggleButton"
                            data-nav="topbar/none/scan"
                            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.barcode_scanner'|trans }}">
                        <svg class="nav-i" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#nav-i-upc-scan"/></svg>
                    </button>
                {% else %}
                    <button type="button" class="site-search-scan site-search-scan--locked"
                            data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#membersExclusiveModal"
                            data-nav="topbar/none/scan_locked"
                            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.barcode_scanner'|trans }}">
                        <svg class="nav-i" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#nav-i-upc-scan"/></svg>
                        <i class="ci-locked site-search-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="site-search-close" data-action="click->global-search#closeSearchBar" data-nav="topbar/none/close_search" aria-label="{{ 'nav.bar.close_search'|trans }}">
                <svg class="nav-i" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#nav-i-x-lg"/></svg>
            </button>
        </div>
        {#- The results panel: phones - fixed under the bar down to the bottom bar; desktop - a dropdown under the field.
            display: none until the search is open (critical CSS). A tap on its empty part closes the search. -#}
        <div class="site-search-panel" data-global-search-target="panel">
        {% endif %}

        {#- "Pages & settings" (MENU-03): filled in the browser, kept by every Live re-render -#}
        <div class="nav-search-results" data-nav-search-results data-nav-search-target="results" data-live-ignore hidden></div>

        {% if this.query %}
            <div class="global-search-results" data-skip-morph data-barcode-scanner-target="results">
                <h3 class="h6 mb-2"><i class="bi-people"></i> {{ 'menu.players'|trans }}</h3>

                {% if computed.players|length == 0 %}
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">{{ 'global_search.no_player_found'|trans }}</p>
                {% endif %}

                {% for player in computed.players %}
                    <span class="pb-1 pe-3 d-inline-block">
                        <a href="{{ path('player_profile', {playerId: player.playerId}) }}">
                            {% if logged_user.profile is not null and player.playerId in logged_user.profile.favoritePlayers %}
                                <i class="ci-star-filled text-warning"></i>
                            {% endif %}

                            {{ highlight(player.playerName, this.query) }}
                            <code class="text-muted">#{{ highlight(player.playerCode|upper, this.query) }}</code>
                            {% if player.playerCountry is not null %}
                                <small class="shadow-custom fi fi-{{ player.playerCountry.name }}"></small>
                            {% endif %}
                        </a>
                    </span>
                {% endfor %}

                <hr class="my-2">

                <h3 class="h6 mb-2"><i class="bi-puzzle"></i> {{ 'menu.puzzles_overview'|trans }}</h3>

                {% if computed.puzzle|length == 0 %}
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">{{ 'global_search.no_puzzle_found'|trans }}</p>
                {% endif %}

                {% for puzzle in computed.puzzle %}
                    <div class="shadow" data-press="layer">
                        <div class="d-flex py-2">
                            <div style="width: 90px;">
                                <a data-turbo-frame="_top" href="{{ path('puzzle_detail', {puzzleId: puzzle.puzzleId}) }}">
                                    {{ lazy_puzzle_image(
                                        puzzle.puzzleImage,
                                        'puzzle_small',
                                        'puzzle_img_alt'|trans({'%puzzle%': puzzle.manufacturerName ~ ' ' ~ puzzle.puzzleName}),
                                        loop.index,
                                        90,
                                        'rounded-2',
                                        88,
                                        puzzle.puzzleImageRatio
                                    ) }}
                                </a>
                            </div>

                            <div class="ps-2 flex-grow-1">
                                <div class="puzzle-name">
                                    <a class="text-decoration-underline fs-sm low-line-height d-inline-block mb-1" data-turbo-frame="_top" href="{{ path('puzzle_detail', {puzzleId: puzzle.puzzleId}) }}">
                                        {{ highlight(puzzle.puzzleName, this.query) }}
                                        {#
                                            {% if puzzle.puzzleId in puzzles_solved_by_user %}<i class="ms-1 text-decoration-none ci-check-circle text-success"></i>{% endif %}
                                        #}
                                    </a>

                                    <br>
                                    {{ include('puzzle/_name.html.twig', {
                                        name: puzzle.puzzleName,
                                        alternative_names: puzzle.puzzleAlternativeNames,
                                        query: this.query,
                                        class: 'mb-1',
                                    }, with_context = false) }}
                                    <small class="fw-bold">{{ 'pieces_count'|trans({ '%count%': puzzle.piecesCount })|raw }}</small>
                                </div>

                                <div class="fs-sm manufacturer-name">
                                    {{ puzzle.manufacturerName }}
                                    {% if puzzle.puzzleIdentificationNumber is not null %}
                                        <small class="text-muted">{{ highlight(puzzle_brand_codes(puzzle.puzzleIdentificationNumber)|join(', '), this.query) }}</small>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>

                                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between text-nowrap puzzle-times-info">
                                    <small>{{ 'puzzle_solved_times'|trans({'%count%': puzzle.solvedTimes})|capitalize|raw }}</small>

                                    <br class="d-none d-md-block">
                                    {% if ranking[puzzle.puzzleId] is defined %}
                                        <small><i class="ci-user"></i> {{ ranking[puzzle.puzzleId].time|puzzlingTime }}</small>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>

                                <div class="text-md-center">
                                    {% for tag in tags[puzzle.puzzleId] ?? [] %}
                                        <span class="badge text-wrap bg-primary rounded-pill mt-1"><i class="ci-diamond"></i> {{ tag.name }}</span>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}

                {% if computed.puzzle|length > 0 %}
                    <p class="text-center mt-2 mb-0">
                        <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-turbo-frame="_top" href="{{ path('puzzles', {search: this.query}) }}">
                            {{ 'global_search.show_all_puzzles'|trans({'%count%': computed.puzzleCount}) }}
                        </a>
                    </p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if member %}
        <div id="search-scan-{{ nav_surface }}" data-barcode-scanner-target="wrapper" class="global-search-barcode-scan d-none" data-live-ignore></div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if not menu %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
